WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-ES

00:00:07.048 --> 00:00:12.137
Hello, welcome back to the
Wheel of Life home retreat,

00:00:15.223 --> 00:00:19.769
where this horse race
is coming to an end.

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:26.818
We've reached
session 24 of 25,

00:00:28.445 --> 00:00:34.909
and this session is called
"My Hair on Fire,"

00:00:36.244 --> 00:00:42.208
and the picture you see here is of a guy
whose clothes and hair are both on fire.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:52.927
Let's go to the Tibetan and we can see
why we use this image.

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:57.599
DES NA BSHES SPRING LAS

00:00:57.599 --> 00:00:58.975
BSHES SPRING refers to

00:00:58.975 --> 00:01:04.606
a famous book
by Arya Nagarjuna,

00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:09.110
it is called "The Letter to the King".  I'm

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.072
sorry, "Letter to a Friend".

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:17.702
His friend was King Udayibhadra.

00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:22.791
And he sent this letter to the king.

00:01:25.126 --> 00:01:26.753
I think it's interesting

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:32.759
that Pabongka Rinpoche quotes it
so frequently in his lam rim,

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:38.306
because I was fortunate enough

00:01:38.306 --> 00:01:42.685
to work a lot on that text
when I was very young.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:48.650
My friend Art Engle,
a fellow student,

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:55.573
a dear fellow student,
and my teacher translated that book.

00:01:58.827 --> 00:02:03.832
And what I realized
while studying that book

00:02:05.166 --> 00:02:08.336
is that it's a lam rim, okay?

00:02:08.878 --> 00:02:11.506
So we tend to think
that the lam rim,

00:02:11.506 --> 00:02:14.676
the teachings of the steps of the path,
began in Tibet,

00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:17.178
but that is not true.

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:26.896
This book in Sanskrit
is called Suhrleka.

00:02:29.107 --> 00:02:32.986
Written by Nagarjuna
almost 2,000 years ago, it

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:38.449
is a kind of
very beautiful lam rim.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:47.542
And Pabongka Rinpoche
quotes two famous verses here.

00:02:50.128 --> 00:02:52.839
MGO'AM GOS LA GLO BUR ME SHOR NA

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:58.011
Suppose your clothes
or hair suddenly catch on fire.

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:06.561
And by the way, this happened with someone
during my three-year retirement.

00:03:09.063 --> 00:03:13.610
Someone got too close to
the fire

00:03:13.735 --> 00:03:14.861
and...

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:18.114
their clothes caught fire,

00:03:18.239 --> 00:03:21.075
and that's very, very dangerous.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.328
So you have to...

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:26.623
We were taught in the Boy Scouts

00:03:27.248 --> 00:03:31.085
that you have to knock them down
immediately,

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:34.130
push them down,

00:03:35.423 --> 00:03:37.759
and then roll them away.

00:03:38.843 --> 00:03:40.887
So that's what I did.

00:03:41.763 --> 00:03:45.016
DE DAG PHYIR BZLOG BGYI BA
BTANG NAS KYANG

00:03:45.808 --> 00:03:52.607
If your clothes or hair catch fire, you
won't do other things.

00:03:55.485 --> 00:04:00.698
You will immediately do everything you can
to stop the fire.  You're

00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:04.452
not going to say, "Oh, my hair
is on fire,

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:08.706
but I think I'll
finish my coffee first."

00:04:12.794 --> 00:04:15.171
We have a job like that.

00:04:16.297 --> 00:04:18.758
YANG SRID MED PAR BGYI

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:24.806
We want to extinguish the fire
of rebirth.

00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:31.562
We have very little time
in this life.

00:04:32.313 --> 00:04:34.691
As long as you are healthy,

00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:37.694
as long as you can still meditate,

00:04:38.069 --> 00:04:40.697
as long as your mind
is still clear,

00:04:41.322 --> 00:04:44.784
as long as you still have food
and a place to stay, you do

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:51.332
n't have time to do
many other things.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.711
This fire is burning you now.

00:04:56.254 --> 00:05:02.635
Then you have to stop everything else
and try to put out this fire.

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:06.848
DI LAS CHES MCHOG DGOS PA
GZHAN MA MCHIS There is

00:05:06.848 --> 00:05:11.102
nothing more important
that you have to do in your life.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.188
And...

00:05:14.772 --> 00:05:20.528
in general, I've followed this
in my life.

00:05:24.032 --> 00:05:29.787
And the fact is, if you want to put out
that fire, you

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:37.754
won't have time to do
many other things.

00:05:39.756 --> 00:05:47.722
So you may have to give up
many things that other people do in their lives.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:53.978
And I've been doing that
for almost 50 years,

00:05:55.688 --> 00:06:05.782
and I can report, I can tell you, I
believe I made the right decision.

00:06:07.241 --> 00:06:09.410
So, for example,

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:12.246
I'm really bad at buying
birthday presents

00:06:12.246 --> 00:06:15.166
for my family.

00:06:18.586 --> 00:06:22.340
And it's not that I don't love them.
We love each other very much.

00:06:24.425 --> 00:06:27.178
But if I dedicate the time
to going to the store

00:06:27.178 --> 00:06:29.597
to choose a gift
for each member of the family—

00:06:29.597 --> 00:06:32.392
we are a large family—

00:06:36.437 --> 00:06:40.608
then I won't have time
to do those three things:

00:06:40.608 --> 00:06:43.111
Vipashyana,

00:06:43.111 --> 00:06:47.865
trying to understand
dependence and emptiness;

00:06:49.784 --> 00:06:51.619
shamatha,

00:06:51.619 --> 00:06:55.123
do my meditation practice
every day, without breaking it

00:06:55.123 --> 00:06:58.709
to go to the store
to buy birthday presents.

00:07:02.672 --> 00:07:05.800
And then there is the daily study
and practice of morality,

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:09.470
which I need to support
my meditation.

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:17.437
Then Nagarjuna says here...

00:07:19.355 --> 00:07:22.608
Nagarjuna says here:

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:26.112
"It's as if your hair
is on fire. There

00:07:26.696 --> 00:07:30.241
is nothing more important
at this moment."

00:07:30.241 --> 00:07:33.828
Put out that fire
and then do other things.

00:07:35.538 --> 00:07:39.792
Become a Buddha
and then buy birthday presents.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:43.629
TSUL KHRIMS DAG DANG
How are you going to put out this fire?

00:07:44.839 --> 00:07:48.509
TSUL KHRIMS DAG DANG
SHES RAB BSAM GTAN GYIS

00:07:48.509 --> 00:07:52.263
You must use TSUL KHRIMS,
which means

00:07:52.263 --> 00:07:57.560
treating other people gently,
with kindness, without harming other people;

00:07:58.769 --> 00:08:03.566
SHES RAB, that wisdom
which understands emptiness,

00:08:06.235 --> 00:08:09.489
vipashyana being the highest form;

00:08:10.865 --> 00:08:17.788
and then shamatha, a good
and stable state of meditation.

00:08:18.706 --> 00:08:24.545
If you remember, these are the three parts
of the woodcutter. A

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:28.716
sharp axe, which is wisdom;

00:08:30.885 --> 00:08:37.725
good focus like that still flame,
to strike in the right place;

00:08:40.561 --> 00:08:45.900
and then two strong arms of morality
to wield the axe.

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:52.698
Then, if you use those three,

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:58.454
you will reach MYA NGAN 'DAS.
The text says MYA NGAN 'DAS, Nirvana.

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:03.751
Also called ZHI BA,
which means peace.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.712
Also called DUL BA,

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:11.092
which means that you have
complete control over yourself.  same.

00:09:12.843 --> 00:09:16.430
Also called
DRI MED PA'I GO 'PHANG,

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:21.227
the state beyond
all impurities.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:30.444
Also called MI RGA, you
no longer have to grow old.

00:09:31.445 --> 00:09:35.700
MI 'CHI means you
no longer have to die.

00:09:35.992 --> 00:09:38.119
ZAD MI 'TSAL means:

00:09:38.119 --> 00:09:45.751
This life and this purity will
never end.

00:09:47.044 --> 00:09:51.465
In "Letter to a Friend,"

00:09:51.465 --> 00:09:55.094
the last line is strange.

00:09:55.803 --> 00:10:00.016
SA CHU ME RLUNG NYI ZLA
BRAL THOB MDZOD

00:10:00.016 --> 00:10:04.854
You should try to reach
that place

00:10:06.314 --> 00:10:13.279
where you have no earth,
water, fire, and wind,

00:10:14.739 --> 00:10:17.158
and by the way, also...

00:10:17.158 --> 00:10:20.494
get rid of the sun
and the moon.

00:10:20.995 --> 00:10:25.666
Now... that last line...

00:10:25.666 --> 00:10:32.715
I thought we should take a little detour
on the journey, which I like to do.

00:10:34.842 --> 00:10:37.136
What does that last line mean?

00:10:37.136 --> 00:10:42.266
The other words for Nirvana
are easy.

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:45.686
Peace means, of course,

00:10:45.686 --> 00:10:50.733
"I no longer have negative emotions;
it is peaceful."

00:10:51.525 --> 00:10:55.529
DUL BA means, "I have self-control."
Of course.

00:10:56.364 --> 00:11:02.036
DRI MA MED PA, no more problems in my body,
no more problems in my mind; I do

00:11:02.703 --> 00:11:04.789
n't have to grow old, I don't have to

00:11:04.789 --> 00:11:06.999
die,

00:11:06.999 --> 00:11:10.836
my pure life continues
forever.

00:11:11.712 --> 00:11:13.714
That's it.  Easy.

00:11:13.714 --> 00:11:16.384
But what does
SA CHU ME RLUNG NYI ZLA BRAL mean?

00:11:16.384 --> 00:11:22.014
What does it mean to conquer earth,
water, fire, wind...

00:11:22.014 --> 00:11:24.558
sun and moon? I

00:11:26.727 --> 00:11:30.272
went to find some commentaries.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:36.779
The one I enjoyed the most
was by a great Mongolian author, his name is

00:11:39.031 --> 00:11:43.119
Chuje Ngawang Pelden.

00:11:43.744 --> 00:11:48.124
Chuje means Lord of Dharma.

00:11:48.916 --> 00:11:52.461
He lived about...
I think 200 years ago.

00:11:53.504 --> 00:11:55.715
And...

00:11:55.715 --> 00:11:59.385
Here is his commentary
on that last line.

00:12:00.803 --> 00:12:02.471
So we go deeper,

00:12:02.471 --> 00:12:04.265
and that's what we do,
and that's why

00:12:04.265 --> 00:12:08.436
this teaching
of Lam Rim is so slow.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:14.233
SA CHU ME RLUNG NYI ZLA
BRAL THOB MDZOD.

00:12:14.233 --> 00:12:19.029
He says, "What
about this strange last line?"

00:12:20.948 --> 00:12:24.201
So, there's a Mongolian master.

00:12:26.203 --> 00:12:30.916
He says, "What about
this strange last line?"

00:12:31.959 --> 00:12:34.086
He says: SA CHU MED RLUNGS.

00:12:34.086 --> 00:12:36.630
These four elements.

00:12:37.798 --> 00:12:39.675
That's easy.

00:12:39.675 --> 00:12:43.345
DI LA BYED means:
It refers to the four elements.

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:46.849
And it means that after you
reach Nirvana

00:12:46.849 --> 00:12:49.435
or become a Buddha, you

00:12:50.686 --> 00:12:53.898
don't have this normal body

00:12:54.899 --> 00:12:58.319
made of these four elements.

00:12:59.653 --> 00:13:02.990
You have  What we call a
rainbow body.

00:13:05.034 --> 00:13:07.912
Why is it called a
rainbow body?

00:13:07.912 --> 00:13:10.831
From a distance,

00:13:10.831 --> 00:13:14.960
a rainbow appears to have a shape
and colors,

00:13:17.171 --> 00:13:21.008
but when you get close
to the rainbow,

00:13:21.467 --> 00:13:24.553
you can pass your hand through it,

00:13:24.595 --> 00:13:28.015
and the physical body of a Buddha
is similar.

00:13:30.017 --> 00:13:36.190
Now here's the part I like
about his commentary; it's very sweet.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:42.154
He says: NYI ZLA. Why does he mention
the sun and the moon?

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:44.949
KHYAD PAR 'PHAGS BSTOD LAS.

00:13:44.949 --> 00:13:46.992
This is called...

00:13:46.992 --> 00:13:49.411
This is a famous book called

00:13:49.411 --> 00:13:55.876
"Praise of the One
Who Is Exaltedly Superior."

00:13:56.377 --> 00:13:59.046
It's a poem.

00:13:59.463 --> 00:14:02.675
No. He's going to quote, he's going
to quote a book.

00:14:02.675 --> 00:14:04.927
It's a famous eulogy.

00:14:04.927 --> 00:14:11.559
Eulogy means a poem of praise,
which is found in the Tengyur.

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:14.687
And he says:

00:14:14.687 --> 00:14:18.941
NE TZOS NYI MA BRNGOL NAS NO,

00:14:18.941 --> 00:14:21.235
which
is probably a mistake...

00:14:21.235 --> 00:14:23.988
here everything is misspelled
and misspelled.

00:14:24.071 --> 00:14:26.907
So I had to replace
a lot of words, okay?

00:14:26.907 --> 00:14:29.785
But he says:

00:14:29.785 --> 00:14:34.039
THAR PA MCHIS PAR BSHAD
CES GRAGS.

00:14:34.039 --> 00:14:38.085
The  Parrot, the green parrot...
that talking bird

00:14:40.212 --> 00:14:43.382
pecked the sun

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:47.052
with its beak

00:14:48.929 --> 00:14:52.683
and then they say it reached
Nirvana.

00:14:53.934 --> 00:14:56.353
What's all that about? This is

00:14:56.353 --> 00:14:59.273
supposed to explain
the sun and the moon. There is

00:14:59.273 --> 00:15:02.610
no sun anymore, there is no
moon anymore.

00:15:03.777 --> 00:15:06.363
Forget the sun and the moon.

00:15:07.781 --> 00:15:11.035
DRANG SRONG means

00:15:11.035 --> 00:15:13.120
a Hindu saint, his

00:15:15.915 --> 00:15:19.668
name is RGYAS PA'I BU,

00:15:22.796 --> 00:15:26.216
with some miraculous powers,

00:15:26.216 --> 00:15:31.513
took a parrot or became
a parrot. It's not clear.

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:36.810
He flew to the sun,

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:40.064
pecked it, and made a hole in
the sun,

00:15:42.524 --> 00:15:46.946
and then that saint
went into the hole

00:15:47.196 --> 00:15:49.990
and reached Nirvana.

00:15:51.033 --> 00:15:53.243
Then this Mongolian master,

00:15:53.327 --> 00:15:56.080
who is a great, great master,

00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:04.129
says that Shantideva...
Oh, sorry, the book by Nagarjuna,

00:16:05.005 --> 00:16:07.967
they are criticizing this idea

00:16:07.967 --> 00:16:13.889
that Nirvana is a place
on the other side of the moon or something like that.

00:16:19.728 --> 00:16:21.981
Then he criticizes...

00:16:21.981 --> 00:16:25.943
He says sun and... when the book says,
"You are free from the sun and the moon," it

00:16:26.026 --> 00:16:27.945
means you are free
from this silly idea

00:16:27.945 --> 00:16:31.281
about what Nirvana is.

00:16:37.746 --> 00:16:41.417
I found another interesting one...

00:16:42.459 --> 00:16:48.674
Yes, here's a
Rendawa's comment.

00:16:50.843 --> 00:16:56.724
Rendawa was a Sakya master
who was Tsongkhapa's teacher.

00:16:59.476 --> 00:17:02.396
And when he explains the sun
and the moon,

00:17:03.188 --> 00:17:05.733
PHYI ROLA PA KHA CIG.
Some non-Buddhists say

00:17:05.733 --> 00:17:06.775
YANG PHYI ROL PA KHA CIG.

00:17:06.775 --> 00:17:09.945
It is at the end of his quote.

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:19.371
KHA BA DUNG RGYA SPOS BA
ZHO BA MO MU TIG MDOG.

00:17:19.788 --> 00:17:21.206
He says: "Some people think

00:17:21.206 --> 00:17:26.754
that when you reach Nirvana
you enter a white light.

00:17:28.964 --> 00:17:32.926
"It's like the color of snow,

00:17:33.093 --> 00:17:36.513
" or the color of a white seashell,

00:17:37.765 --> 00:17:41.977
"or like the color of a pearl
or the color of yogurt.

00:17:44.938 --> 00:17:49.068
And it feels like an umbrella is
covering you."

00:17:51.195 --> 00:17:55.449
And these are all strange ideas
about Nirvana.

00:17:57.743 --> 00:18:00.788
So he says,
when this book says,

00:18:00.788 --> 00:18:03.957
"You go beyond the sun
and the moon," it

00:18:05.959 --> 00:18:08.796
means you go beyond
these silly ideas about,

00:18:08.796 --> 00:18:12.091
"Oh, Nirvana is like a big white umbrella


00:18:12.091 --> 00:18:17.429
and you stay under the umbrella
like in a sun donut."

00:18:18.138 --> 00:18:22.309
Sun donut, with a hole
in the middle.

00:18:34.988 --> 00:18:37.950
And you may say
that those are just stupid old ideas

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:42.371
from some weird groups
in India,

00:18:45.499 --> 00:18:50.170
but you could examine what ideas
you have about what Nirvana is.

00:18:53.507 --> 00:18:59.805
And perhaps it's not so different from
the white umbrella.

00:19:02.599 --> 00:19:05.018
Now, just for fun,
something I enjoy doing,

00:19:05.018 --> 00:19:09.022
I thought you might like to go
to a...

00:19:09.356 --> 00:19:14.528
This is a book by
Pabangka Rinpoche himself.

00:19:17.072 --> 00:19:19.950
And this is a beautiful kind
of book genre,

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:23.203
it's a type of literature.

00:19:24.371 --> 00:19:28.208
And his name is DRIS LAN.  DRIS LAN
stands for questions and answers.

00:19:29.084 --> 00:19:30.878
So, even in this course,

00:19:30.878 --> 00:19:35.132
we're going to do a special masterclass

00:19:37.593 --> 00:19:42.931
and I'll take your questions
and answer them live.

00:19:45.559 --> 00:19:49.146
In addition, in the extended course,

00:19:49.146 --> 00:19:54.735
they will be able to ask questions directly
online or in person,

00:19:55.319 --> 00:20:00.115
or via the internet to ACI senior teachers
.

00:20:06.038 --> 00:20:08.540
But in ancient times,

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:13.754
someone would sit there
carving the question.

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:20.344
So here is a question that someone
actually asked Pabongka Rinpoche

00:20:20.344 --> 00:20:23.430
probably about 100 years ago.

00:20:26.266 --> 00:20:29.937
BSHES SPRING LAS, SA CHU ME RLUNG
NYI ZLA BRAL THOB MDZOD

00:20:29.937 --> 00:20:33.857
So what about the last line
of "Letter to a Friend"

00:20:33.857 --> 00:20:39.446
that talks about: "You reached Nirvana
where you no longer have sun or moon"?

00:20:43.992 --> 00:20:46.828
Ah, and here is
Pabongka's own answer,

00:20:46.828 --> 00:20:49.706
because he didn't answer it, he did
n't ask the question in his lam rim,

00:20:49.748 --> 00:20:54.795
but someone asked him later:
"What was that line?"

00:20:58.173 --> 00:21:00.968
And by the way,
this is the great benefit

00:21:00.968 --> 00:21:04.179
of us having
5 million pages

00:21:04.179 --> 00:21:09.268
of digitized deeds
from the last 33 years.

00:21:15.649 --> 00:21:19.194
And I know many of you
watching this lam rim are helping

00:21:19.194 --> 00:21:23.991
to organize the fundraising
for that digitization.

00:21:29.496 --> 00:21:31.915
I wanted to thank you for that.

00:21:31.915 --> 00:21:36.712
And the reason I can go into more detail
with you

00:21:37.671 --> 00:21:41.008
is because of your fundraising.

00:21:41.008 --> 00:21:47.180
And it definitely helps the poor people
around the world whom we train.

00:21:47.306 --> 00:21:49.933
For 33 years.

00:21:51.059 --> 00:21:54.062
And it's beautiful now, some of those ladies I
met

00:21:54.062 --> 00:21:58.942
in the first year of this project

00:22:00.902 --> 00:22:03.572
had children,

00:22:03.572 --> 00:22:10.370
and now those children are working
alongside them on the computer.

00:22:12.039 --> 00:22:13.623
Okay, so here it says:

00:22:13.623 --> 00:22:14.875
PHYI ROL PA 'GA' ZHIG GIS

00:22:14.958 --> 00:22:18.003
'BYUNG BA BZHI DANG NYI ZLA SOGS LA
THOB BYA MTHAR THUG TU' DZIN PA DANG.

00:22:18.003 --> 00:22:21.715
It says: "Some people...

00:22:21.715 --> 00:22:25.427
"strange old schools,

00:22:27.596 --> 00:22:30.390
" "they think Nirvana
is like a white light

00:22:30.390 --> 00:22:35.979
" where you go and stay
in this white light.

00:22:37.564 --> 00:22:39.191
THAR PA GZUGS CAN DU 'DOD PA.

00:22:39.191 --> 00:22:44.404
These are strange ideas
that Nirvana is a physical place.

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:52.371
But if you really want to go to the
real Nirvana,

00:22:53.080 --> 00:22:56.583
you need those three trainings:

00:22:57.000 --> 00:22:58.585
morality,

00:22:58.585 --> 00:23:00.212
concentration,

00:23:00.212 --> 00:23:02.881
and wisdom.

00:23:06.093 --> 00:23:10.931
Yes, I have to say
that a lot of people think

00:23:12.099 --> 00:23:17.646
that if you study this section
that we've covered with 25 classes,

00:23:20.023 --> 00:23:22.359
if you study it well,

00:23:22.692 --> 00:23:25.445
then you will reach Nirvana.

00:23:26.029 --> 00:23:27.906
And you know,

00:23:27.906 --> 00:23:30.033
people think it's...

00:23:30.033 --> 00:23:33.620
like you're
really drunk.

00:23:33.954 --> 00:23:35.956
And you're like that...

00:23:36.832 --> 00:23:39.793
for the rest of the time

00:23:39.793 --> 00:23:43.380
and you're like in another space.

00:23:44.005 --> 00:23:47.092
This is not Nirvana at all.

00:23:47.676 --> 00:23:49.970
The definition of Nirvana:

00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:53.140
NYON SGRIB MA LUS PAR
SPANGS PA'I SO SOR BRTAG 'GOG

00:23:53.140 --> 00:23:55.892
Basically, you get rid
of your anger, jealousy,

00:23:55.892 --> 00:24:00.230
and other negative emotions
forever.

00:24:04.067 --> 00:24:06.194
That's nirvana.

00:24:06.194 --> 00:24:10.991
So Xiaoping, for example,
was translating for me here yesterday,

00:24:13.493 --> 00:24:18.999
and she's translating for me here today,
in the same place.

00:24:19.583 --> 00:24:25.213
So it's possible that
she reached nirvana last night,

00:24:25.422 --> 00:24:29.384
and she wouldn't look any different.

00:24:29.885 --> 00:24:33.472
Okay? So you have to understand that.

00:24:34.014 --> 00:24:37.017
The person sitting next to you

00:24:37.017 --> 00:24:42.939
might have reached nirvana last night
because of these great classes.

00:24:45.108 --> 00:24:50.363
And they won't change; their
outward appearance won't change. They

00:24:51.072 --> 00:24:58.455
no longer have negative emotions,
and you can't make them angry.

00:25:00.415 --> 00:25:03.585
Okay, let's go back to lam rim.

00:25:04.711 --> 00:25:06.463
But that kind of deepening

00:25:06.463 --> 00:25:07.839
is only possible

00:25:07.839 --> 00:25:14.930
because we have a database
that we built over 33 years. I

00:25:17.557 --> 00:25:24.314
reckon we still have 117 years to go,

00:25:25.148 --> 00:25:32.322
so I hope you'll continue to help,
and I thank you for your help so far.

00:25:33.573 --> 00:25:38.161
Especially the friends
from the Gold Club.

00:25:39.579 --> 00:25:42.707
CES GSUNGS PA LTAR, SKYES BU 'TRAE
GI NYAMS  SU BLANG BYA NI

00:25:42.707 --> 00:25:44.626
Well, what is it that...

00:25:44.626 --> 00:25:49.089
people with this average motivation,

00:25:50.257 --> 00:25:52.676
what are they trying to achieve?

00:25:53.468 --> 00:25:59.933
They just want to stop suffering
forever for themselves.

00:26:00.225 --> 00:26:03.937
Well, what
should they focus on?

00:26:04.062 --> 00:26:11.361
LHAG PA'I BSLAB PA GSUM
Those three extraordinary trainings:

00:26:12.612 --> 00:26:15.240
always being kind
to other people,

00:26:16.449 --> 00:26:19.911
doing your meditation
every morning,

00:26:20.120 --> 00:26:24.249
and studying, studying,
studying about emptiness.

00:26:24.916 --> 00:26:26.334
Now,

00:26:26.334 --> 00:26:29.713
GSUM YIN PAS SKYES BU CHEN PO'I
CHOS SKOR MI 'KHRID NA

00:26:29.713 --> 00:26:32.090
SKABS' DIR BSLAB PA GSUM
KA 'CHAD DGOS

00:26:32.090 --> 00:26:36.052
Now, if I weren't going to teach
you

00:26:36.052 --> 00:26:39.347
the highest path, the

00:26:39.347 --> 00:26:41.975
Mahayana path,

00:26:43.977 --> 00:26:47.981
if this were just a series
of lectures

00:26:47.981 --> 00:26:52.152
on how to attain Nirvana,
not Buddhahood...

00:26:55.488 --> 00:26:57.490
Of course, Buddhahood
means

00:26:57.490 --> 00:27:00.160
that your whole body changes,
your mind changes,

00:27:00.160 --> 00:27:06.333
you can help people
on billions of planets at the same time.

00:27:15.967 --> 00:27:20.555
Nirvana just means,
"I, a person here on this couch,

00:27:20.555 --> 00:27:25.018
feel no anger, no jealousy."

00:27:27.354 --> 00:27:32.776
That by  True, that means you've stepped off
the Wheel of Life.

00:27:35.695 --> 00:27:40.492
But not everyone who attains Nirvana
attains Buddhahood.

00:27:41.951 --> 00:27:45.664
Buddhahood, your whole being changes.

00:27:48.375 --> 00:27:51.086
And you are able to help

00:27:51.086 --> 00:27:53.546
countless beings
on countless planets

00:27:53.546 --> 00:27:55.882
at the same time.

00:27:59.052 --> 00:28:01.930
Then Pabongka Rinpoche says,

00:28:02.931 --> 00:28:08.311
"I'm not finished with you
after you finish this Nirvana thing."

00:28:09.813 --> 00:28:12.607
"I have a great plan for you.

00:28:13.024 --> 00:28:15.318
We're going to go to the teachings
of the greater path,

00:28:15.318 --> 00:28:18.196
the Mahayana teachings,

00:28:18.196 --> 00:28:21.366
where you learn to become
a Buddha."

00:28:22.158 --> 00:28:25.453
"To reach that Buddhahood
you will also need

00:28:25.453 --> 00:28:29.708
"these same three trainings.

00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:36.756
"So, if I weren't going to teach you
this higher path,

00:28:37.757 --> 00:28:41.803
if I were only teaching you
about Nirvana,

00:28:41.803 --> 00:28:48.017
well, I would teach you the details
of those three trainings today.

00:28:50.395 --> 00:28:56.609
But, I am going to teach you
those higher goals,

00:28:57.694 --> 00:29:03.450
so I think we'll save
two of those trainings for later.

00:29:04.909 --> 00:29:09.664
Like shamatha training,
deep meditation."

00:29:09.789 --> 00:29:15.086
"Vipashyana training, a
special vision of emptiness. I

00:29:16.796 --> 00:29:20.175
will teach them to you later."

00:29:20.633 --> 00:29:24.179
And by the way,
that's my plan too.

00:29:25.054 --> 00:29:27.807
After we finish
this book, because...

00:29:27.807 --> 00:29:32.645
Pabongka Rinpoche doesn't spend much time
on shamatha and vipashyana in this book,

00:29:32.645 --> 00:29:34.814
a little, but not much.

00:29:43.114 --> 00:29:50.538
At the end of this book we will go to:
The Great Book on the Steps of the Path.

00:29:52.582 --> 00:29:54.918
Lam Rim Chenmo.

00:29:55.627 --> 00:30:02.091
That will take us 13 more years
to finish.

00:30:03.802 --> 00:30:07.972
We will only do the
shamatha and vipashyana parts.

00:30:07.972 --> 00:30:10.809
That part alone
will take 13 years.

00:30:14.687 --> 00:30:15.980
Okay?  So...

00:30:15.980 --> 00:30:20.026
So I'm telling you, and Pabongka
is telling you,

00:30:20.026 --> 00:30:26.032
"We'll get there later, we'll cover those two training sessions
later."

00:30:27.534 --> 00:30:28.952
So I'm going to...

00:30:28.952 --> 00:30:31.329
TSUL KHRIMS KYI BSLAB PA
RTZAL DU BTON means:

00:30:31.329 --> 00:30:33.581
"Let's focus

00:30:33.581 --> 00:30:37.043
on an ethical way of life."

00:30:39.003 --> 00:30:40.588
That's the PHYAG BZHES here.

00:30:40.588 --> 00:30:45.885
PHYAG BZHES means: "That is the tradition
of the high lamas at this time."  We are

00:30:45.885 --> 00:30:54.394
only focusing on morality because we will teach you
shamatha and vipashyana later.

00:30:55.061 --> 00:31:01.943
Then he quotes again
Letter to a Friend of Nagarjuna.

00:31:03.236 --> 00:31:05.947
KHRIMS NI RGYU DANG MI RGYU'I
SA BZHIN DU YON TAN

00:31:05.947 --> 00:31:09.075
KUN GYI GZHI RTEN LAGS PAR GSUNGS,

00:31:09.075 --> 00:31:15.123
How can I describe the practice
of leading an ethical life?

00:31:20.920 --> 00:31:23.506
Think about this planet Earth.

00:31:23.506 --> 00:31:30.305
The great earth, the enormous, enormous, enormous,
all the countries resting on this planet.

00:31:32.932 --> 00:31:38.563
RGYU DANG MI RGYU'I SA
is an old, old joke.

00:31:38.980 --> 00:31:40.940
The earth of this planet

00:31:40.940 --> 00:31:47.238
supports everything that moves
and everything that does not move.

00:31:50.199 --> 00:31:54.120
So now
we're in Sedona, Arizona.  I do

00:31:54.913 --> 00:31:55.955
n't know if you can see,

00:31:55.955 --> 00:31:58.833
but these red mountains in the background
are very, very famous.

00:31:58.833 --> 00:32:03.129
Six million people
visit us every year.

00:32:06.424 --> 00:32:12.221
And the earth, patiently and silently,
holds those mountains all day and all night.

00:32:18.853 --> 00:32:24.484
And if you look out the window
you'll see some cars moving.

00:32:25.610 --> 00:32:31.157
And the earth also patiently sustains them
day and night.

00:32:33.368 --> 00:32:36.287
So whether things
move like cars,

00:32:36.287 --> 00:32:39.207
or don't move
like red mountains,

00:32:39.207 --> 00:32:42.919
the earth is very patient
and just holds them up.

00:32:49.968 --> 00:32:55.014
And Nagarjuna says:
"Your morality is like this."

00:32:56.349 --> 00:33:00.019
Okay, you want to meditate,

00:33:00.019 --> 00:33:04.065
you want to have direct perception
of emptiness...

00:33:04.065 --> 00:33:08.069
By the way, meditation
is like mountains,

00:33:08.486 --> 00:33:12.824
and seeing emptiness directly
is like cars.

00:33:12.824 --> 00:33:16.577
But someone patient and calm

00:33:16.577 --> 00:33:21.541
always has to be there underneath.
The base.

00:33:25.670 --> 00:33:27.880
And that is morality.

00:33:27.880 --> 00:33:31.050
ZHES PA LTAR YON TAN
THAMS CAD KYI GZHI YIN PAS

00:33:31.884 --> 00:33:36.931
Being kind to other people
is the basis of every good quality.

00:33:40.893 --> 00:33:44.480
TSUL KHRIMS RNAM PAR DAG PA GAL CHE
Therefore,

00:33:45.023 --> 00:33:49.902
never hurting any other person
is extremely important.

00:33:51.821 --> 00:33:53.990
'DI NI SANGS RGYAS KYI
BSTAN PA'I RTZA BA

00:33:54.073 --> 00:33:58.995
Treating people well
is the root of all Buddhism.

00:34:01.664 --> 00:34:03.916
BSRUNG NA PHAN YON CHE

00:34:03.916 --> 00:34:06.127
If you maintain an
ethical way of life,

00:34:06.127 --> 00:34:11.257
if you are kind to other people,
the benefits that come to you are incredible.

00:34:16.304 --> 00:34:18.765
MA BSRUNGS NA NYES
DMIGS KYANG SHIN TU CHE STE

00:34:18.765 --> 00:34:21.100
And if you don't...

00:34:21.100 --> 00:34:23.936
maintain an ethical lifestyle
and hurt others, you ca

00:34:23.936 --> 00:34:29.275
n't imagine the kind of problems you
're creating for yourself.

00:34:33.112 --> 00:34:35.656
And I'll tell you another...

00:34:35.656 --> 00:34:38.785
important thing that
Buddha said about...

00:34:38.785 --> 00:34:42.163
being kind to other people.

00:34:47.460 --> 00:34:48.920
If people

00:34:48.920 --> 00:34:51.672
in any city or country

00:34:51.672 --> 00:34:57.470
are upholding their commitment
to be kind to others,

00:35:00.932 --> 00:35:02.433
then Buddha said,

00:35:02.433 --> 00:35:05.645
"Buddhism is there."

00:35:06.562 --> 00:35:12.443
And if they are not maintaining that kind of commitment
to being kind to other people,

00:35:14.862 --> 00:35:19.575
then you can't say
that Buddhism has reached that point.

00:35:23.746 --> 00:35:25.998
Then repeat:

00:35:26.749 --> 00:35:30.461
DGE SLONG 'DUL BA' DZIN PA
BSTAN PA YOD LA

00:35:31.587 --> 00:35:35.800
If there is a person in a city

00:35:36.384 --> 00:35:38.010
maintaining

00:35:38.010 --> 00:35:41.013
a way of life where he never
harms other people,

00:35:41.013 --> 00:35:45.935
then Buddhism exists
in that city.

00:35:50.731 --> 00:35:53.192
So, even if there is...

00:35:53.192 --> 00:35:57.363
tantra, high secret teachings

00:35:58.489 --> 00:36:00.741
reach that city

00:36:00.741 --> 00:36:05.246
and everyone is ringing their bells,

00:36:07.999 --> 00:36:12.170
but if they are not being kind
to other people,

00:36:13.254 --> 00:36:15.423
then we can say

00:36:15.423 --> 00:36:19.051
that Buddhist teachings
did not reach that place.

00:36:20.595 --> 00:36:27.185
Even though people there practice the
highest teachings, they are not moral.

00:36:32.940 --> 00:36:35.026
Therefore,

00:36:35.026 --> 00:36:38.154
the Buddha himself said:

00:36:38.154 --> 00:36:45.620
NGA NI MYA NGAN 'DAS GYUR NA,
'DI NI KHYOD KYI STON PA ZHES

00:36:45.620 --> 00:36:48.247
After I disappear
from this world,

00:36:48.247 --> 00:36:51.918
after I reach
my final Nirvana,

00:36:54.337 --> 00:36:57.924
part of me will remain
in this world,

00:36:58.341 --> 00:37:02.178
and that part of me
will be your teacher forever.

00:37:03.554 --> 00:37:07.934
And that's keeping your vows
and not hurting other people.

00:37:08.726 --> 00:37:12.438
So, if a person in this world

00:37:13.064 --> 00:37:19.362
is keeping their commitment
to never harm other people,

00:37:19.946 --> 00:37:25.910
then Buddha said,
"You can say that I am still here."

00:37:29.038 --> 00:37:31.123
Final prayer

00:37:31.123 --> 00:37:33.084
of this

00:37:33.084 --> 00:37:35.044
series.

00:37:37.755 --> 00:37:43.010
And then, the twenty-fifth session
will be a review.

00:37:44.804 --> 00:37:45.554
RANG RGYUD...

00:37:45.554 --> 00:37:48.432
So listen
and let it be like a mantra for you.

00:37:48.432 --> 00:37:52.436
Listen to the words.
It's a blessing.

00:37:54.230 --> 00:37:56.983
RANG RGYUD KYI TSUL KHRIMS
LA STON PA'I SKU TSAB YIN SNYAM DU

00:37:56.983 --> 00:38:00.278
GCES SPRAS BYAS NAS BSRUNG DGOS

00:38:00.945 --> 00:38:04.573
Most of you
listening

00:38:04.573 --> 00:38:09.495
have probably taken
some kind of Buddhist vows,

00:38:09.495 --> 00:38:13.332
at least the ten good deeds:

00:38:13.332 --> 00:38:15.126
Do not kill;  do

00:38:15.126 --> 00:38:17.003
not steal;

00:38:17.003 --> 00:38:20.047
not to harm other people's relationships,

00:38:20.047 --> 00:38:23.009
etc.

00:38:23.009 --> 00:38:27.972
We can say that in your stream of consciousness

00:38:27.972 --> 00:38:33.019
you are maintaining
this lifestyle

00:38:33.019 --> 00:38:37.106
where you are kind
to other people.

00:38:37.106 --> 00:38:39.900
Then Pabongka says,

00:38:39.900 --> 00:38:42.778
"So we can say,

00:38:44.196 --> 00:38:47.283
well, you don't have to be perfect,

00:38:47.283 --> 00:38:52.121
but those of you who are trying
to keep your book six times over,

00:38:52.121 --> 00:38:58.044
and since you heard about this teaching
about the seeds,

00:38:59.837 --> 00:39:05.301
you are trying to be kinder
to other people.

00:39:05.301 --> 00:39:11.724
As long as you are generally, imperfectly,
trying to be kind to other people,

00:39:11.724 --> 00:39:14.643
not perfectly,

00:39:16.562 --> 00:39:20.816
we can say that the Buddha
is alive within you.

00:39:22.860 --> 00:39:24.737
And GCES SPRAS means,

00:39:24.737 --> 00:39:27.615
'Take good care of that Buddha.'

00:39:27.615 --> 00:39:32.036
It is the most precious thing in your life.

00:39:32.703 --> 00:39:36.290
That is the end of session 24.

00:39:37.666 --> 00:39:44.924
In session 25, we will do a review
of all 25 sessions. See you soon

00:39:46.175 --> 00:39:47.927
.

00:39:47.927 --> 00:39:55.309
I know, Xiaoping, that you are very tired
and have been working very hard, and thank you for translating.

00:39:55.309 --> 00:39:56.977
Yay! You

00:39:57.561 --> 00:39:59.021
didn't translate 'yay.'

00:39:59.021 --> 00:40:01.023
(Xiaoping)
Oh, yay!"

